<style>
  .rail {
    position: fixed;
    right: 14px;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    z-index: 20;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  /*
   * The rail sits directly on the paper page, not inside an instrument —
   * ticks are ink chrome, not phosphor. `--cyan` (a Task-1-review carried
   * finding) aliased to `--green`, which measures 1.45:1 against paper —
   * functionally invisible.
   *
   * Task 3 carried ruling: an earlier pass here used `--leader`/`--clay`
   * for the two tick states, but those are large-graphic tokens (3:1
   * floor) and a 7px tick is non-text UI, not large text/graphics — it
   * still has to clear WCAG 1.4.11's 3:1 non-text floor, which `--leader`
   * (2.1:1 on paper) and `--clay` (2.79:1 on paper) both fail. `--ink-dim`
   * (4.8:1) and `--clay-ink` (5.1:1) are the paper-world tokens that
   * actually clear it.
   */
  .rail a {
    display: block;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: var(--ink-dim);
    transition: background 0.25s, transform 0.25s;
  }
  .rail a.on {
    background: var(--clay-ink);
    transform: scale(1.35);
  }
  .rail a:focus-visible {
    outline: 1px solid var(--ink);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Matches the storyboard's own breakpoint: the rail competes with thumb
     reach on narrow viewports, and scroll position is self-evident there
     without a chrome element pointing at it. */
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .rail { display: none; }
  }
</style>
